"FRAGMENT\")\n    38\t\n    39\t\n    40\t# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n    41\t#  fused_linear_apply custom op\n    42\t# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n    43\t#\n    44\t# Hot path is deliberately allocation-lean.  All per-(layer, comp_id)\n    45\t# state is pre-bound at install time into a flat list on the loader\n    46\t# (``dm._fused_reg``) so the runtime impl looks up everything with a\n    47\t# single integer index — no per-call tuple-key construction, no\n    48\t# ``getattr`` chains, no scratch-cache 5-tuples, no extra stream wraps.\n    49\t#\n    50\t# Registry entry layout (positional list, indexed by\n    51\t# ``layer_id * 4 + comp_id``):\n    52\t#\n    53\t#     [0] K               int  — comp.K (cached so we skip int(comp.K))\n    54\t#     [1] M               int  — comp.M\n    55\t#     [2] compressor      object\n    56\t#     [3] comp_ref        CompressedXxxTensor\n    57\t#     [4] fde             frozen_decomp_event (None if no wait needed)\n    58\t#     [5] kde             kernel_done_event   (None if no record needed)\n    59\t#     [6] scratch_by_N    dict[int, dict[str, Tensor]] — per-N scratch\n    60\t#     [7] comp_c          pre-extracted compressor binding\n    61\t#     [8] wd_begin        WDecomp begin event (None if timing is disabled)\n    62\t#     [9] wd_end          WDecomp end event   (None if timing is disabled)\n    63\t#     [10] leaf_module    Linear used by the large-prefill dense fallback\n    64\t#     [11] ww_begin       weight-wait begin event (None if timing is disabled)\n    65\t#     [12] ww_end         weight-wait end event   (None if timing is disabled)\n    66\t#\n    67\t# A list/index access is ~2-3× faster than dict[tuple] lookup and does\n    68\t# not allocate the tuple key on every call.  All but ``scratch_by_N``\n    69\t# are immutable bindings populated at install time.\n    70\t\n    71\t\n    72\t_REG_ENTRY_SLOTS = 4  # qkv, o, gate_up, down\n    73\t_SCRATCH_CACHE_N_MAX = 512\n    74\t\n    75\t\n    76\tdef _fused_linear_apply_impl(x: torch.Tensor, layer_id: int,\n    77\t                             comp_id: int, M: int) -> torch.Tensor:\n    78\t    \"\"\"Dispatch the registered compressor's ``linear_apply``.\n    79\t\n    80\t    The compressor decides the actual GEMM strategy.  For P4Flat we\n    81\t    currently route through ``decompress + F.linear`` (cuBLAS) which\n    82\t    benchmarks ~2.6× faster than the custom fused MM kernel at\n    83\t    decode-sized N — the kernel's BN=128 tiling wastes compute when\n    84\t    the activation N is small.  See ``P4FlatCompressor.linear_apply``.\n    85\t\n    86\t    Registry entry layout (see DualMemoryLoader._maybe_install_fused_mm):\n    87\t        [0] K          int\n    88\t        [1] M          int   (unused — also passed as op arg)\n    89\t        [2] compressor object\n    90\t        [3] comp_ref   CompressedXxxTensor\n    91\t        [4] fde        frozen_decomp_event or None\n    92\t        [5] kde        kernel_done_event or None\n    93\t        [6] scratch_by_N (legacy slot, retained for ZipServ/DietGPU)\n    94\t        [7] comp_c     pre-extracted ``comp._c`` (legacy slot)\n    95\t        [8] wd_begin   WDecomp begin event (or None) — timed by linear_apply\n    96\t        [9] wd_end     WDecomp end event   (or None)   only on the fallback\n    97\t                        decompress path (fused path leaves them unrecorded).\n    98\t        [10] leaf      Linear used by the large-prefill dense fallback\n    99\t        [11] ww_begin  weight-ready wait begin event (or None)\n   100\t        [12] ww_end    weight-ready wait end event (or None)\n   101\t    \"\"\"\n   102\t    from tiered_serve.dual_memory_loader import DualMemoryLoader\n   103\t\n   104\t    dm = DualMemoryLoader._v1_dm_ref\n   105\t    # During the real ``profile_run`` and the cudagraph WARMUP the wrapper skips\n   106\t    # weight streaming, so the per-decode staging the fused op reads is stale.\n   107\t    # offload's bulk sign_mantissa is then OOB → IMA; frozen_split's sign_mantissa\n   108\t    # is HBM-permanent so it survives, but the guard is harmless there.  Return\n   109\t    # the output SHAPE only there; do NOT short-circuit during the cudagraph\n   110\t    # CAPTURE (the REAL op must bake in — the per-step data is streamed before\n   111\t    # each decode replay).  Capture is detected via the dedicated\n   112\t    # ``_v1_fused_capturing`` flag (vllm/compilation/cuda_graph.py).\n   113\t    if dm is not None and (getattr(dm, \"is_profiling\", False)\n   114\t                           or getattr(dm, \"is_graph_warming_up\", False)):\n   115\t        _capturing = (getattr(dm, \"_v1_fused_capturing\", False)\n   116\t                      or torch.cuda.is_current_stream_capturing())\n   117\t        if not _capturing:\n   118\t            return x.new_zeros(*x.shape[:-1], M)\n   119\t\n   120\t    entry = dm._fused_reg[layer_id * _REG_ENTRY_SLOTS + comp_id]\n   121\t    fde = entry[4]\n   122\t    kde = entry[5]\n   123\t    ww_begin = entry[11]\n   124\t    ww_end = entry[12]\n   125\t\n   126\t    # SINGLE STREAM: decompress+GEMM (or the fused kernel) run on the CURRENT\n   127\t    # stream — the cudagraph capture/replay stream under capture, exec_stream\n   128\t    # eagerly.  No comp_stream fork (capture-illegal; see ZipServ fused_mm /\n   129\t    # decompress).  ``fde`` is the per-component weight-ready barrier, recorded\n   130\t    # on the producer stream (load_weight_stream for frozen_split H2D). Waiting\n   131\t    # it on the current stream is capture-safe and orders the decode after the\n   132\t    # H2D in both captured and eager execution.\n   133\t    cur = torch.cuda.current_stream(x.device)\n   134\t    _capturing = (getattr(dm, \"_v1_fused_capturing\", False)\n   135\t                  or torch.cuda.is_current_stream_capturing())\n   136\t    if fde is not